@@ -0,0 +1,110 @@
+# ScaleAlign RF-DETR-2XL continuation
+
+This research path tests whether prediction-derived continuous scale state improves fixed-budget query allocation in
+the official RF-DETR-2XL architecture.
+
+## Supported scope
+
+RF-DETR-2XL from `rfdetr-plus==1.0.2` is fixed at 880 x 880, 300 queries, five decoder layers, and the NAS-selected
+DINOv2-B architecture. Its projector exposes only `P4`, so this branch implements and tests:
+
+- ESM: `a = 0.5 * (log(w) + log(h))` and `g = log(w) - log(h)`, with stopped box gradients.
+- SGQG: deterministic greedy allocation balancing foreground logits and KL scale-distribution coverage.
+- QCD and proposal R@K diagnostics, plus single-level box-attention misalignment (BAM).
+
+It does not claim cross-level SAA or SMR evidence. `saa_enabled=True` is rejected for the official single-level 2XL
+configuration. Full cross-level SAA must be evaluated in a detector with at least two decoder feature levels.
+
+## Environment
+
+Use the RF-DETR commit recorded by `scripts/run_equal_budget.py` and `rfdetr-plus==1.0.2`:
+
+```bash
+uv sync --all-groups --extra plus
+```
+
+COCO must use the official layout and counts:
+
+```text
+COCO_ROOT/
+  train2017/                              # 118,287 image records
+  val2017/                                # 5,000 image records
+  annotations/instances_train2017.json
+  annotations/instances_val2017.json
+```
+
+## Matched continuation
+
+Both branches start from the same official `rf-detr-xxlarge.pth`, run 12 epochs, and keep resolution, queries, decoder
+depth, optimizer settings, seed, batch/accumulation budget, augmentation, and evaluation settings identical.
+
+```bash
+python scripts/run_equal_budget.py \
+    --dataset-dir "$COCO_ROOT" \
+    --checkpoint "$RFDETR_2XL_CHECKPOINT" \
+    --branch both \
+    --dry-run
+
+python scripts/run_equal_budget.py \
+    --dataset-dir "$COCO_ROOT" \
+    --checkpoint "$RFDETR_2XL_CHECKPOINT" \
+    --branch both
+```
+
+The launcher validates official COCO counts, hashes the checkpoint once, rejects accidental output overwrite, and
+records commit/config/runtime provenance. `--resume` requires and restores each branch's existing `last.ckpt`.
+
+## Local ScaleAlign-only run
+
+This host also has a treatment-only configuration bound to the verified COCO 2017 dataset at
+`data/coco`. The official checkpoint is stored at
+`weights/rf-detr-xxlarge.pth` with registered MD5 `e3204689c1f0280427e4c33e6a2ac6cd`.
+
+Start the 12-epoch ESM+SGQG continuation run with:
+
+```bash
+cd .
+.venv-scalealign/bin/python scripts/run_scalealign_local.py
+```
+
+The launcher refuses CPU fallback, a corrupt checkpoint, an invalid COCO layout, or accidental reuse of a nonempty
+output directory. Continue an interrupted run from its full Lightning state with:
+
+```bash
+.venv-scalealign/bin/python scripts/run_scalealign_local.py --resume
+```
+
+This single treatment run is useful for engineering validation, but it is not a substitute for the matched baseline
+branch when reporting a causal AP improvement.
+
+The primary one-epoch multi-scale treatment uses the released single-P4 2XL model as a frozen teacher for the first
+`0.25` epoch only, with classification and box weights `0.25` and `1.0`. The multiplier decays per training batch, so
+the warmup remains effective inside a one-epoch run and the teacher is released for the remaining 75% of batches.
+
+## Diagnostics and benchmark
+
+Enable `scalealign.diagnostics` for validation-only capture. Save each detached batch dictionary as a separate `.pt` shard
+containing `proposals`, `targets`, optional `qcd`, and optional per-layer `boxes`, `sampling_locations`, and
+`attention_weights`. Shards are reduced in lexical filename order and only one shard is resident at a time:
+
+```bash
+python tools/analyze_scalealign.py \
+    --captures captures/ \
+    --checkpoint checkpoint.pth \
+    --output diagnostics.json
+```
+
+Legacy `.pt` files containing a list of captures require `--allow-legacy-monolith`. This compatibility mode loads the
+entire file into memory, emits a runtime warning, and records the unbounded storage mode in the JSON report.
+
+Compare finished checkpoints with batch-one 880 x 880 FP16, 100 warmups, and 500 synchronized CUDA iterations:
+
+```bash
+python tools/benchmark_scalealign.py \
+    --baseline-checkpoint experiments/scalealign_2xl/baseline/checkpoint.pth \
+    --scalealign-checkpoint experiments/scalealign_2xl/scalealign/checkpoint.pth \
+    --output experiments/scalealign_2xl/benchmark.json
+```
+
+The benchmark reports PyTorch eager CUDA latency and must not be compared directly with the published TensorRT T4
+latency. Final reporting requires AP, AP_S/AP_M/AP_L, GPU hours, peak memory, latency, QCD, R@K, and BAM for both runs.
